              ],
              "start": 0,
              "end": 5,
              "quote": "中国山水画"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "tr-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:2",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:2"
              ],
              "start": 6,
              "end": 102,
              "quote": "几千年来，山水画一直是中国艺术的重要组成部分。中国画家通常画的不是真实的地方，而是想象中的、理想化的山水。在中国，山与宗教联系在一起，因为山高高耸向天际。因此人们相信，观赏山的画作对心灵有益。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "tr-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:3",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:3"
              ],
              "start": 103,
              "end": 162,
              "quote": "山水画被看作书法的延伸。它色彩克制，通常以墨在纸上作画，只施少量水彩。这些画以手卷、册页、扇面等不同形式装裱在丝绸上。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "tr-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:4",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:4"
              ],
              "start": 163,
              "end": 301,
              "quote": "到唐代后期，山水画已经发展成一个独立的画种。这种艺术形式被推向了极致，画家们借此表达与自然融为一体的愿望。关于中国哪一幅山水画最早让这种艺术形式诞生，长期以来一直存在争论，但许多艺术评论家确实认为《洛神赋图》是这类画作中的第一幅。这幅画一直象征着人们心中与自然合一的隐秘渴望。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "tr-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:5",
              "sourceParagraphIds": [
                "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:5"
              ],
              "start": 302,
              "end": 401,
              "quote": "直到今天，自然的意象一直是艺术家的灵感来源。中国的艺术表达深深烙上了自然世界的印记。这些画也真实描绘了画家内心的感受、思想以及挣扎。观赏中国山水画时，我们永远不应停止欣赏和理解中国山水艺术非凡的美。"
            }
          ]
        },
        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "For thousands of years, landscape paintings, or Shan Shui Hua, have been a major part of Chinese art. Chinese artists don’t usually paint real places but imaginary, idealized landscapes. In China, mountains are associated with religion because they reach up towards the heavens. People therefore believe that looking at paintings of mountains is good for the soul."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "Landscape paintings are seen as an extension of calligraphy. The colors are restrained and the paintings are usually created in ink on paper, with a small amount of watercolor. They are mounted（装裱）on silk in different formats such as handscrolls, album leaves and fan paintings."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "By the late Tang Dynasty, landscape painting had evolved into an independent genre. The genre of such an art form was taken to extreme heights, with painters expressing their desire to be at one with nature. There have been long-held arguments over which landscape painting in China was the first one to bring this art form to life, but many art critics do believe The Nymph of the Luo River to be the first of its kind. The painting has stood as symbols of man’s hidden desire to be united with nature."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:5",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-jiangsu-subei-eight-cities-2025-05:grammar-fill:5",
            "text": "Images of nature have remained a source of inspiration for artists down to the present day. Chinese artistic expression is deeply imprinted with images of the natural world. The paintings are also a true portrayal of their artists’ inner feelings and thoughts as well as struggles. Viewing Chinese landscape paintings, we should never stop appreciating and understanding the extraordinary beauty of Chinese landscape art."
          }
        ],
